More Vulnerabilities That Can Be Paid (441–450)
441. Improper API Endpoint Authorization
API Endpoint Authorization Bypass
Some API endpoints fail to check user permissions correctly, allowing attackers to perform unauthorized actions.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $9,000
442. Insecure Token Transmission
Authentication Token Exposure
Authentication tokens transmitted through insecure channels such as URLs or unencrypted requests.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
443. Insecure Mobile App Storage
Mobile Application Data Storage Vulnerability
Sensitive user data stored insecurely within mobile applications.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
444. Improper OAuth Redirect Handling
OAuth Redirect Misconfiguration
OAuth implementations fail to validate redirect URIs, enabling account takeover.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $10,000
445. Insecure Password Reset Flow
Password Reset Workflow Vulnerability
Password reset processes allow attackers to reset passwords without proper verification.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $8,000
446. Insecure Temporary Access Tokens
Temporary Token Security Weakness
Temporary tokens used for authentication remain active longer than intended.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $5,000
447. Improper Handling of HTTP Referer Header
HTTP Referer Header Information Leakage
Sensitive URLs leak through the Referer header to external domains.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $4,000
448. Unsecured Internal API Gateway
Internal API Gateway Exposure
Internal API gateways accessible from the internet without proper restrictions.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $9,000
449. Improper File Download Validation
File Download Authorization Bypass
Applications fail to verify user permissions before allowing file downloads.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
450. Unrestricted API Query Parameters
API Query Manipulation Vulnerability
Attackers manipulate API query parameters to retrieve unintended data.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
